{
  "schema": "dlive-api-fixtures/1",
  "source": "docs/bridge-client-api-v1.md (accepted 2026-08-25; amended 2026-09-07, spec 1a: broadcast-driven mirror 1.2)",
  "note": "Authority for the Client API wire shapes, BOTH sides: the monorepo server replays requests and asserts responses; the Companion module mocks the server from the same file (vendored by tools/sync_fixtures.sh, monorepo -> module repo — the REVERSE of the protocol fixtures). Matching rules: response bodies are SUBSET-matched (extra server keys are allowed — additive changes don't bump v1, spec §11); '<str>'/'<int>' match any value of that type; '<lane>' is substituted with the lane_id registered by the most recent hello case; 'sends' asserts the exact console-bound hex the request must produce. A request's 'headers' and 'content_type' are sent as given (a body is sent as application/json unless 'content_type' says otherwise); an empty 'sends' asserts that nothing reached the console. Never edit a case to make a test green — change the spec first, then both sides.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "info.ok",
      "request": {"method": "GET", "path": "/api/v1/info"},
      "response": {"status": 200, "body": {
        "v": 1, "session": "main", "api": 1, "mirror": "1.2",
        "capabilities": {"raw": true, "fade": true, "query": true,
                          "fader_db": true, "send_level": true,
                          "mirror_from_broadcast": true},
        "return_port_policy": "broadcasts", "seq": "<int>"}}
    },
    {
      "id": "info.console",
      "note": "Spec §1b (2026-10-19, MIDI Bridge 1.4.90): info and hello carry the active driver's client profile. On the dLive it is exactly Talk Light's and Pilot Tone's fallback (shared/bridge_link.fallback_profile) at the bridge's base channel. Additive: a client that ignores it is unaffected.",
      "request": {"method": "GET", "path": "/api/v1/info"},
      "response": {"status": 200, "body": {"console": {
        "driver": "dlive", "title": "dLive",
        "scenes": {"noun": "Scene", "first": 1, "last": 500},
        "triggers": {"noun": "SoftKey", "id_prefix": "cc"},
        "actions": {"noun": "Action", "fields": [
          {"id": "cc", "label": "CC #", "min": 0, "max": 127},
          {"id": "value", "label": "Value", "min": 0, "max": 127}]}}}}
    },
    {
      "id": "info.console.digico",
      "note": "MIDI Bridge 1.4.106: the console block's `actions` declares an Action's fields, and {\"op\": \"action\", <field id>: value} takes them. The DiGiCo SD's is one Macro number, from 1; the dLive's is cc and value (info.console). `family` names the console the case runs against; the SD is offered in test builds only.",
      "family": "digico",
      "request": {"method": "GET", "path": "/api/v1/info"},
      "response": {"status": 200, "body": {"console": {
        "driver": "digico", "title": "DiGiCo",
        "actions": {"noun": "Macro", "fields": [
          {"id": "macro", "label": "Macro", "min": 1, "max": 999}]}}}}
    },
    {
      "id": "console.objects.not_supported",
      "note": "Spec §1b (MIDI Bridge 1.4.91): GET /console/objects lists every object with its name, colour and stereo layout, from the SQ's MixPad session. The dLive answers 501 not_supported until 1.4.92, and a client falls back to the query op (shared/console_scan.read_console_objects returns None). Nothing reaches the console.",
      "request": {"method": "GET", "path": "/api/v1/console/objects?timeout_ms=100"},
      "response": {"status": 501, "body": {
        "ok": false, "error": {"code": "not_supported"}}},
      "sends": []
    },
    {
      "id": "hello.ok",
      "request": {"method": "POST", "path": "/api/v1/hello",
                  "body": {"v": 1, "session": "main",
                           "name": "Fixture Lane", "kind": "companion"}},
      "response": {"status": 200, "body": {
        "v": 1, "session": "main", "lane_id": "<str>",
        "capabilities": {"raw": true}, "seq": "<int>"}}
    },
    {
      "id": "hello.bad_kind",
      "request": {"method": "POST", "path": "/api/v1/hello",
                  "body": {"name": "x", "kind": "toaster"}},
      "response": {"status": 400, "body": {
        "ok": false, "error": {"code": "bad_kind"}}}
    },
    {
      "id": "cmd.mute.input1.on",
      "request": {"method": "POST", "path": "/api/v1/cmd",
                  "body": {"v": 1, "session": "main", "lane_id": "<lane>",
                           "cid": "fx1",
                           "intent": {"op": "mute", "type": "input",
                                       "index": 1, "on": true}}},
      "response": {"status": 200, "body": {"cid": "fx1", "ok": true}},
      "sends": ["9b 00 7f"]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmd.fader.db_unity",
      "request": {"method": "POST", "path": "/api/v1/cmd",
                  "body": {"lane_id": "<lane>", "cid": "fx2",
                           "intent": {"op": "fader", "type": "input",
                                       "index": 1, "db": 0.0}}},
      "response": {"status": 200, "body": {"cid": "fx2", "ok": true}},
      "sends": ["bb 63 00 bb 62 17 bb 06 6b"]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmd.action.pool_cc",
      "request": {"method": "POST", "path": "/api/v1/cmd",
                  "body": {"lane_id": "<lane>", "cid": "fx7",
                           "intent": {"op": "action", "cc": 20,
                                       "value": 127}}},
      "response": {"status": 200, "body": {"cid": "fx7", "ok": true}},
      "sends": ["bb 14 7f"]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmd.action.out_of_pool_cc_allowed",
      "request": {"method": "POST", "path": "/api/v1/cmd",
                  "body": {"lane_id": "<lane>", "cid": "fx8",
                           "intent": {"op": "action", "cc": 80,
                                       "value": 0}}},
      "response": {"status": 200, "body": {"cid": "fx8", "ok": true}},
      "sends": ["bb 50 00"],
      "note": "A&H's safe pool is advisory — Pilot Tone Trigger ships CC 80, outside it. The API must not reject what an operator has legitimately bound; the monitor annotates instead."
    },
    {
      "id": "cmd.raw",
      "request": {"method": "POST", "path": "/api/v1/cmd",
                  "body": {"lane_id": "<lane>", "cid": "fx3",
                           "intent": {"op": "raw", "hex": "9b 05 7f"}}},
      "response": {"status": 200, "body": {"cid": "fx3", "ok": true}},
      "sends": ["9b 05 7f"]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmd.unknown_lane",
      "request": {"method": "POST", "path": "/api/v1/cmd",
                  "body": {"lane_id": "ln_000000", "cid": "fx4",
                           "intent": {"op": "mute", "type": "input",
                                       "index": 1, "on": true}}},
      "response": {"status": 401, "body": {
        "ok": false, "error": {"code": "unknown_lane"}}}
    },
    {
      "id": "cmd.send_level.ok",
      "note": "Ungated 1.1.8. Was cmd.send_level.capability_off (409). The gate's condition was the send LV<->dB law, which the 5 Sept sweep measured identical to the fader's at all 128 steps (report 3.1); spec change recorded in STATUS.md before this case moved.",
      "request": {"method": "POST", "path": "/api/v1/cmd",
                  "body": {"v": 1, "session": "main", "lane_id": "<lane>",
                           "cid": "fx5",
                           "intent": {"op": "send_level", "type": "input",
                                      "index": 1, "dest_type": "mono_aux",
                                      "dest_index": 1, "level": 100}}},
      "response": {"status": 200, "body": {"cid": "fx5", "ok": true}},
      "sends": ["f0 00 00 1a 50 10 01 00 0b 0d 00 0d 00 64 f7"]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmd.unsupported_op",
      "request": {"method": "POST", "path": "/api/v1/cmd",
                  "body": {"lane_id": "<lane>", "cid": "fx6",
                           "intent": {"op": "peq", "type": "input",
                                       "index": 1}}},
      "response": {"status": 400, "body": {
        "ok": false, "error": {"code": "unsupported_op"}}}
    },
    {
      "id": "stream.resync",
      "request": {"method": "GET", "path": "/api/v1/stream?cursor=-1"},
      "response": {"status": 409, "body": {
        "ok": false, "error": {"code": "resync"}}},
      "note": "cursor=-1 is always older than the ring's oldest entry"
    },
    {
      "id": "lane.delete.unknown",
      "request": {"method": "DELETE", "path": "/api/v1/lane/ln_000000"},
      "response": {"status": 404, "body": {
        "ok": false, "error": {"code": "unknown_lane"}}}
    },
    {
      "id": "security.origin",
      "request": {"method": "POST", "path": "/api/v1/hello",
        "headers": {"Origin": "https://some-website.example"},
        "content_type": "text/plain;charset=UTF-8",
        "body": {"v": 1, "session": "main", "name": "web page", "kind": "companion"}},
      "response": {"status": 403, "body": {
        "ok": false, "error": {"code": "forbidden_origin"}}},
      "note": "#105, spec §4: a web page's cross-site POST. text/plain needs no CORS preflight; it got a lane until MIDI Bridge 1.3.1."
    },
    {
      "id": "security.origin.cmd",
      "request": {"method": "POST", "path": "/api/v1/cmd",
        "headers": {"Origin": "https://some-website.example"},
        "body": {"lane_id": "<lane>", "cid": "fx9", "intent": {"op": "raw", "hex": "9b 00 7f"}}},
      "response": {"status": 403, "body": {
        "ok": false, "error": {"code": "forbidden_origin"}}},
      "sends": [],
      "note": "#105: Input 1 mute on reached the console from a web page until MIDI Bridge 1.3.1."
    },
    {
      "id": "security.host",
      "request": {"method": "GET", "path": "/api/v1/info",
        "headers": {"Host": "attacker.example"}},
      "response": {"status": 403, "body": {
        "ok": false, "error": {"code": "forbidden_host"}}},
      "note": "DNS rebinding: a hostname that resolves to 127.0.0.1 must still be refused."
    },
    {
      "id": "cmd.bad_content_type",
      "request": {"method": "POST", "path": "/api/v1/cmd",
        "content_type": "text/plain",
        "body": {"lane_id": "<lane>", "cid": "fx10", "intent": {"op": "raw", "hex": "9b 00 7f"}}},
      "response": {"status": 415, "body": {
        "ok": false, "error": {"code": "bad_content_type"}}},
      "sends": [],
      "note": "A cross-site page can send text/plain without a preflight; application/json it cannot."
    }
  ]
}
